   "evidence": "Writing `m = x + t \u2022 (y - x)`: for `t \u2208 [0,1]` it is the field; for `t > 1`, `y = (1 - 1/t) \u2022 x + (1/t) \u2022 m \u2208 segment \u211d x m`, so `W x m = W x y * W y m` and `W x m * W m y = W x y` by `apply_swap`; for `t < 0`, `x \u2208 segment \u211d m y` with coefficient `-t/(1-t) \u2208 (0,1)`, giving the same conclusion. Mathlib has `line[\u211d, x, y]` (Mathlib/Geometry/Euclidean/Altitude.lean:144) and `segment_eq_image_lineMap` (Mathlib/Analysis/Convex/Segment.lean:216). That the line form is the natural level is visible in the file itself: `IsAxialGauge` (line 307) quantifies over unrestricted `t : \u211d`, and `pathLink_staplePath_eq_transverseLink_of_isAxialGauge` (line 329) instantiates it at `t := s - L`, of either sign.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/TMD/GaugeLink.lean",
   "fix": "Keep `toFun_mul_toFun'` (line 108) segment-only \u2014 it is the weakest constructor obligation \u2014 and export the stronger lemmas: `apply_mul_apply_of_mem_line (W) {x y m} (hm : m \u2208 line[\u211d, x, y]) : W x m * W m y = W x y`, and the corresponding `pathLink_subdivide` with the same hypothesis; derive the segment cases from them (or drop them).",
   "issue": "`apply_mul_apply_of_mem_segment` (and with it `pathLink_subdivide_of_mem_segment`, line 225) is stated only for `m \u2208 segment \u211d x y`, but the two fields imply `W x m * W m y = W x y` for every `m` on the line through `x` and `y`. Downstream path reduction needs the line form: the staple's out-leg `x \u2192 x + L\u2022n` and return leg `x + L\u2022n + w \u2192 x + s\u2022n + w` overlap in opposite senses whenever `|s| < |L|`, i.e. in the physical configuration, so a backtracking corner cannot be reduced with the segment-only lemma.",
   "line": 130
  }
 ],
